            "goal": "Proxy long streaming responses reliably at scale.",
            "opener": "Most responses stream for several seconds. What does that mean for the gateway?",
            "evidence": {
              "strong": "Estimates concurrent open streams from request rate times duration, uses async I/O, falls back only before the first token reaches the client, restarts visibly if a stream fails later, propagates client cancellations upstream, and handles backpressure.",
